=== ROOT CAUSE (QA FINDING F1) ===
preflight declares the services ready on /actuator/health==200 and immediately drives the
throwaway loan. On a COLD Kafka the sample's domain-topic listener has not joined its consumer
group yet, and that listener runs auto.offset.reset=latest, so the verification request is
published into a partition nobody is assigned to and is never delivered.

TIMELINE, all from the archived logs above:
  19:27:15        preflight: all four services HTTP 200 on /actuator/health
  19:27:16.078    loan-application: Started workflow 'loan-preflight-1785864435'
                  -> publishes loans.verification.requests (event seq 2 = requestVerifications)
  19:27:18.284    verification-gateway: 'verification-gateway: partitions assigned:
                  [loans.verification.requests-0,-1,-2]'   <-- 2.2 SECONDS TOO LATE
  auto.offset.reset = latest for that group -> the record is skipped, forever.

RESULT: loan-preflight-1785864435 is stuck WAITING_SIGNAL with exactly 2 events
        (recordApplication, requestVerifications); verification_gateway DB has 0 instances;
        preflight exits 1 at step 7/8.

WHY NO EARLIER REHEARSAL SAW IT: every previous run reused a warm Kafka whose consumer group
already had committed offsets, so auto.offset.reset never applied. It only bites after
'docker compose -f demo/docker-compose.yml down -v' — i.e. exactly the documented cold start
(RUNBOOK.md 'T' section calls down -v 'the CORRECT way to get a truly clean start').

--- ATTRIBUTION of auto.offset.reset to the right group (grepped from the log) ---
ConsumerConfig block at log line 40 (19:27:14.224):  group.id = verification-gateway   auto.offset.reset = latest
  ^ this is the SAMPLE's own @KafkaListener on loans.verification.requests — the one that missed the record
ConsumerConfig block further down:                  group.id = maestro-verification-gateway   auto.offset.reset = earliest
  ^ Maestro's OWN signals topic is safe; it is the sample's domain topics that are not.
